{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuEfbxbKPdmDDT5fDgny","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I created the dashboard and the alert rule, and confirmed both exist in Kibana. The rule has already run once with status `ok`, so its query works. I didn't open the dashboard to check that each chart actually shows data.\n\n**1. What the data holds.** Each record in `kibana_sample_data_logs` is one web request, timed by the `timestamp` field. It records:\n- **Request:** `url`, `request`, `extension`, `referer`, `agent`\n- **Result:** `response` (the HTTP status code, stored as text such as \"503\") and `bytes` (response size)\n- **Client:** `clientip`, `geo.src`, `geo.dest`, `geo.coordinates`, `machine.os`, `machine.ram`\n- **Other:** `tags`, `memory`, `hour_of_day`\n\n**2. Dashboard \"EFF-583fd258 Web logs overview\"** (id `eff-583fd258-web-logs-overview-df153a996a65`) has 7 panels:\n- Total requests\n- Unique visitors (distinct client IPs)\n- Total bytes served\n- Requests over time, split by response code\n- Share of requests by response code\n- Top 10 URLs, with request count and bytes\n- Top 10 source countries by traffic\n\nLink: http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-583fd258-web-logs-overview-df153a996a65\n\n**3. Rule \"EFF-583fd258 5xx spike\"** (id `ef9c43d8-82af-4ec0-a980-3bf414842728`) is a search-based rule that is switched on and checks every minute. It counts requests whose response code starts with \"5\" in the last 5 minutes and fires when there are more than 10. Because the code is stored as text, it matches on the leading \"5\" rather than a number range. I also tagged it `web-logs` and `5xx`.\n\nThe rule has no notification action attached, so when it fires the alert only shows up in Kibana. If you want it to notify you, add a connector such as email or Slack."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creat